# Origin for the a2a-demo.bunsenbrenner.org demo. Caddy terminates TLS; the bridge IS
# the whole web server (dashboard + SSE + the round-triggering endpoint), so this
# Caddyfile's only job is TLS termination + reverse-proxying everything to it -- same
# shape as CADS-auction-demo's Caddyfile.
#
# The cert is issued CORE-side (CADS-Tunnel's scripts/authorize-pipeline.sh, deSEC
# DNS-01) and mounted in as static files -- never an ACME client or DNS credential here.
#
# 2026-08-04: this tunnel dropped back to Gelb (a control-plane restart resets
# the admission-broker's Rot/Gelb/Gruen tracking) -- while Gelb, the edge
# terminates the customer-facing TLS itself with its shared wildcard cert and
# forwards PLAINTEXT to the origin, regardless of whether a valid core-issued
# cert already sits in /certs (Gruen is about the tunnel's admission state,
# not about a cert file merely existing). The old `tls ...` directive made
# Caddy reject that forwarded plaintext ("Client sent an HTTP request to an
# HTTPS server"), confirmed live via curl -v. Same fix already applied to
# webconference-demo's Caddyfile for the identical symptom: auto_https off +
# plain HTTP on :443 while Gelb. Switch back to
# `tls /certs/fullchain.pem /certs/privkey.pem` once this tunnel reaches
# Gruen again (ct-agent certificate).
{
	auto_https off
}

:443 {
	reverse_proxy a2a-demo-bridge:8790
	encode gzip
	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
	}
}
